{"title":"1979 USAMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution  1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution  2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine all non-negative integral solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/8/85867628d5f2c1bb0afe37d28cbc54332f87d8cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n_1,n_2,\\dots , n_{14})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" /> if any, apart from permutations, of the Diophantine Equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/3/3530547f31b70c33947546ab32cbc7d32496c1e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1^4+n_2^4+\\cdots +n_{14}^4=1599$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"209\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution  1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution  1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Recall that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a178d21d2ca133005e1451a379c9d6519dfd235f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_i^4\\equiv 0,1\\bmod{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"134\" height=\"21\" /> for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/b/7eb75ccf06e046206cb4c636a54d7be11d049fbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />. Thus the sum we have is anything from 0 to 14 modulo 16. But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/238d74b61a8a34f6e8f89b5bf7aeacdfcfe823e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1599\\equiv 15\\bmod{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"141\" height=\"13\" />, and thus there are no integral solutions to the given Diophantine equation.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution  2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution  2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, this equation would look like:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/7/4f781cb87004eba8361ae0e450dbdd301bc29832.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n_1^4+n_2^4+\\cdots +n_{14}^4=63F_{16}\\]\" width=\"215\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>We notice that the unit digits of the LHS of this equation should equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/f/02fb1748598da8a8faf3355e295e3a75a7ffe5d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />. In base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the only unit digits of fourth powers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the maximum of these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> terms is 14 <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/f/99fd1c19d4fbfae8ddeee2fafd781648083d9580.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1&#39;s$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/1/891503903dfb5e1d1428856eb5f98d4abdcbd655.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"15\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/1/891503903dfb5e1d1428856eb5f98d4abdcbd655.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"15\" /> is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/f/02fb1748598da8a8faf3355e295e3a75a7ffe5d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />, there are no integral solutions for this equation.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zfChnbMGLVQ?t=4778\">https://youtu.be/zfChnbMGLVQ?t=4778</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO\" title=\"1979 USAMO\">1979 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1979 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1979\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1979 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1979 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1979 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1979 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1979 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016180220\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 125/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1238/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 52/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2886/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.842      1 -total\n 55.90%    6.619      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 42.17%    4.994      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n